  "notes": "API/MCP launch QA (TL-QA-09, TL-QA-10, TL-QA-16; owner asked for this PR 2026-11-23): three MCP templates changed. mcp.investigate_failure v1 -> v2 gives get_test_case its test_id, takes an optional run_id and stops to ask for the run when none is given (no tool finds a run from a test case id); mcp.release_readiness_report v2 -> v3 reads the named release's stored gate first with get_release_gate(evaluate=False) and lists ACTIVE defects; mcp.defect_triage_session v1 -> v2 lists ACTIVE defects (OPEN and IN_PROGRESS). MCP prompts steer an external assistant's tool calls, feed no scored task and are not gated in prompt_eval_recordings: reviewed from source, pinned by mcp/tests/test_mcp_prompt_contract.py, mcp/tests/test_mcp_launch_qa_sweep.py, test_mcp_release_readiness_report_reads_the_gate_verdict and test_mcp_templates_changed_by_the_launch_qa_are_versioned. Gate results are the real offline run: classification, root_cause and release_decision pass; duplicate_detection insufficient_samples as on main. No backend prompt, model choice, routing or watched source changed. Offline golden verdict as computed: insufficient_samples. Recorded as a source-reviewed pass on the owner's approval (2026-11-23), as the 2026-11-22 prompts-no-release-verdict change was.",
